From ed4bf60344237c77d78bff64d4bcc30ed342ee3b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Grische <github@grische.xyz>
Date: Thu, 17 Sep 2026 10:47:39 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] patches/openwrt: fix powerpc32 eBPF JIT miscompilations

The powerpc32 eBPF JIT used by mpc85xx and apm821xx miscompiles two
kinds of programs.

Since 19daf0aef84f ("powerpc/bpf/32: perform three operands ALU
operations") in 6.3, a MOV X is merged into the following ALU operation
on the same register and its own code is dropped - also when that
operation doesn't read the MOV source (the verifier's zero-extension,
self moves, BPF_END, source equal to destination), when an immediate
case reads the old destination, or when a branch lands on the second
instruction. Clang chains bpf_csum_diff() calls through such a pair, so
on a WS-AP3715i CLAT sent packets with bad L4 checksums as soon as
bpf_jit_enable was 1.

In BPF-to-BPF calls, the callee gets the upper half of BPF_REG_1 as its
first argument and returns only the lower half of BPF_REG_0 (both since
51c66ad849a7), and it doesn't receive BPF_REG_5 (since 7dd0e2848764).

Carry the fixes and new test_bpf cases as pending kernel patches until
they are upstream.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
