+From fb35489cf5a8e1b17b6b3367a899ac15608373e0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
+From: Grische <github@grische.xyz>
+Date: Thu, 17 Sep 2026 10:47:06 +0200
+Subject: [PATCH] kernel: fix powerpc32 eBPF JIT miscompilations
+
+The powerpc32 eBPF JIT, used by mpc85xx and apm821xx, generates wrong
+code in two areas.
+
+A MOV X followed by an ALU operation on the same register is emitted as
+one three-operand operation, and the code for the MOV is dropped. Since
+19daf0aef84f ("powerpc/bpf/32: perform three operands ALU operations")
+in 6.3 this also happens when the second instruction does not read the
+MOV source: the verifier's zero-extension, a self move, BPF_END, or an
+operation whose source is the destination register. A few immediate
+cases also read the old destination register, and a branch to the
+second instruction skips the move altogether. Clang passes the result
+of one bpf_csum_diff() to the next with "w5 = w0", which the verifier
+follows with a zero-extension, so on a WS-AP3715i every chained call
+got seed 0 and CLAT sent packets with bad L4 checksums as soon as
+bpf_jit_enable was 1.
+
+BPF-to-BPF calls pass their arguments like helper calls, but the callee
+used the prologue and epilogue of a main program: it treated r3 as a
+32-bit context pointer, so it got the upper half of BPF_REG_1 as its
+first argument, and it returned only the lower half of BPF_REG_0, where
+the caller expects the upper half. Both date back to 51c66ad849a7
+("powerpc/bpf: Implement extended BPF on PPC32"). Since 7dd0e2848764
+("powerpc/bpf/32: BPF prog is never called with more than one arg") the
+callee also doesn't load BPF_REG_5 from the caller's parameter area.
+
+Add the fixes and the matching test_bpf cases as pending patches. They
+are backported from a series that is not upstream yet.
+
+Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
