++Subject: [PATCH 6/6] bpf/tests: Add tests for operations following a MOV
++
++The powerpc32 JIT merges a MOV X with the following operation on the
++same register and got several cases wrong: the verifier's zero
++extension, self moves, BPF_END, operations whose source is the
++destination, 64-bit operations after a 32-bit MOV, sign-extending MOVs,
++immediates that need both halves of the source, and jumps to the second
++instruction.
++
++Add tests that compute each such pair once directly and once with a
++jump in between, which prevents the merge, and compare the results.
++Add the verifier's zero extension, a jump to the second instruction and
++the classic BPF cases "tax; div x" and a jump over "txa" separately.
++
++[ Backport to 6.6: drop the MOVSX and BSWAP cases. 6.6 has neither
++  BPF_MOVSX*_REG() nor BPF_BSWAP(), and its powerpc32 JIT implements
++  neither sign-extending MOVs nor BPF_ALU64 | BPF_END. ]
++
++Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5
